# The saboteur's work is already aboard: the voltage regulator has
# been tampered with, and at fast throttle the operational
# computers' lasers over-charge until the engine dies. Nothing
# warns you here -- push the circuit tester's button in dock and
# it reads "All systems A-O-K," because the tester cannot see
# tampering until it overloads. Probed the at-sea alternative to
# death: the first crawl-space repair attempt out there ALWAYS
# gashes your arm on a sharp corner (scripted, not luck -- four
# shifted timelines, four gashes), the wound blocks the repair
# entirely, Tip refuses to crawl in your place ("You belong in
# there, not I!"), and only Doc at the Aquadome can treat it.
# In dock, before the engine even starts, the same repair is one
# word: "Fixed."

ask tip for tool
open access panel with tool
enter crawl space
fix regulator with tool
exit crawl space
close access panel

turn on engine
open gate
open throttle
e

