# A note on that sonarscope: it renders as inline ASCII because
# Voxam's plain frontend declares "no screen splitting" in the
# header, and Seastalker -- well-behaved junior that it is --
# checks the bit and degrades gracefully instead of calling
# split_window. The honest header working as designed (§11.1);
# the terminal frontend will someday put this display in a real
# upper window.
#
# The yellow light is a freighter entering the harbor, keel at 10
# meters, closing at a square per turn -- and we are headed
# straight at it. The submarine answer: go under. Fifteen meters
# clears the keel with only an orange depth grumble (twenty
# scrapes the shoaling bay floor and turns the warning red), and
# four more squares northeast pass through the opening in the sea
# wall. Open sea, and the first five points.

dive to 15 meters
ne
ne
ne
ne

# With the regulator mended in dock, the crisis the walkthroughs
# stumble through never happens: no rising temperature gauge, no
# red-zone shriek, no wounded crawl-space heroics. The autopilot
# quotes sixty turns to the Aquadome, and fast throttle triples
# the pace without a single degree of complaint.

